{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1732 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3efc207c9c0ebe4ff5715d2e7b7362fe2e3b19d4176e4107e440226c3b2c153f" :edb/db-before-t 1731 :edb/db-after-t 1732 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535044 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:34:52.387Z" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082913 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $2$?" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082913 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $2?$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082913 1145 "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N =\\dfrac{a_1(1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1= -3$ and $r = 2$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (-3(1 - 2^{N}))/(1 - 2) \\\\\n&= ((-3))/((-1))(1 - 2^{N}) \\\\\n&= 3(1 - 2^{N})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082913 1145 "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N =\\dfrac{a_1(1-r^N)}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1= -3$ and $r = 2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-1)}(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =3(1-{2}^{N}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082914 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of the geometric series $2+8+32+\\cdots \\: ?$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082914 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of the geometric series $2+8+32+\\cdots \\:$?" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082914 1145 "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= \\frac{a_{2}}{a_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{2} \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=4$. Substituting these values into the formula for $S_N$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (a_{1}(1 - r^{N}))/(1 - r) \\\\\n&= (2(1 - 4^{N}))/(1 - 4) \\\\\n&= (2(1 - 4^{N}))/((-3)) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}(1 - 4^{N}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(4^{N} - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082914 1145 "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for $S_N$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082915 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $18$ and the common ratio is $3$?" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082915 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $18$ and the common ratio is $3?$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186082915 1145 "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine $a_1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1}r^{n - 1} \\\\\n18 &= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{(3 - 1)} \\\\\n18 &= 9a_{1} \\\\\na_{1} &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=3$. Substituting our values into the formula for $S_N$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (2(1 - 3^{N}))/(1 - 3) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{2}(1 - 3^{N}) \\\\\n&= 3^{N} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 false] [17592186082915 1145 "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine $a_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 18 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 18 & =9{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}\t.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for $S_N$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & ={3}^{N}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186083291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328440 13194139535044 true] [17592186083291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328458 13194139535044 true] [17592186083291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328473 13194139535044 true] [17592186083291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328479 13194139535044 true] [17592186083291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328486 13194139535044 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328447 13194139535044 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328454 13194139535044 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328462 13194139535044 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328466 13194139535044 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328500 13194139535044 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328469 13194139535044 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328476 13194139535044 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328493 13194139535044 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328507 13194139535044 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328514 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328441 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1089 "q-110166" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4}?$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1113 #uuid "6a880b7a-8ca5-52a7-8783-3b205cea8268" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328440 1145 "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=-3$ and $r=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =-4[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}] \\\\  & =4[{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}-1] \\\\  & =4({4}^{-N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328442 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328443 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328444 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328445 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328446 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1041 "selection" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328445 13194139535044 true] [17592186328441 1110 #uuid "90f80dc0-083f-50e5-882c-e4c135b4d07c" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328442 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}({3}^{-N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328442 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328442 1111 #uuid "0ac5aa50-0c14-5498-9e9d-13edf124dc35" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328443 1034 "2({4}^{-N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328443 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328443 1111 #uuid "a41f66c9-f9cd-5cb9-b21e-e7610d1c4a3a" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328444 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}({4}^{-N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328444 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328444 1111 #uuid "59e7aeff-cb57-53a1-a8aa-f73272eaa46e" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328445 1034 "4({4}^{-N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328445 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328445 1111 #uuid "f37b9806-5c64-5cdf-84b2-357f8c4c475e" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328446 1034 "3({3}^{-N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328446 1111 #uuid "133396cc-2531-5640-918a-487469d5bfbe" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328448 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1089 "q-110180" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $4+8+16+\\,⋯?$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1113 #uuid "d39d6ffc-a04a-5e56-a39a-c11a40fa23e8" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328447 1145 "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-4(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328449 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328450 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328451 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328452 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1041 "selection" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328452 13194139535044 true] [17592186328448 1110 #uuid "07669529-00b9-5a8e-b0b8-8ccb8fd15785" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328449 1034 "2({2}^{N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328449 1111 #uuid "bbb37495-c2dc-5fa0-b7c4-528abeffffc3" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328450 1034 "2({4}^{N}-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131