55 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535044 true] [17592186328455 1041 "field-1" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328455 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328457 13194139535044 true] [17592186328455 1110 #uuid "dbffc279-c38d-5246-a3ed-9f0c6e17c348" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328456 1034 "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N+1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328456 1111 #uuid "8dfa61f3-c6e0-57a5-b9f5-2123aa077f4f" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328457 1034 "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N-1)" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535044 true] [17592186328457 1111 #uuid "26f1bf3c-196e-5832-88b4-c1f6d2d4909b" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328459 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1089 "q-276476" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $8$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1113 #uuid "e57a29f2-809a-5f43-832e-20ee9d5d19d0" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328458 1145 "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328460 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328461 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1041 "field-1" 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328460 13194139535044 true] [17592186328459 1110 #uuid "ee4dadc8-1e84-521b-a273-2addeb0ddbd